    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d481-a3">

                <pb facs="1305" n="1299" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1299"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Pacific Station,<lb/>Office Commander in Chief U. S. Naval
                                Force,<lb/>U. S. Flagship Philadelphia</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>,
                            <date calendar="gregorian" when="1894-01-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >January 3, 1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to call the attention of
                    the Department to the admirable discretion exercised by the officers and men of
                    this squadron under the most trying circumstances.</p>
                <pb facs="1306" n="1300" xml:id="pg1300"/>
                <p>Notwithstanding the great parade of preparations for war not one case of
                    misconduct on shore has occurred, and this evidence of perfect discipline has
                    been very favorably commented upon by disinterested parties ashore and
                    afloat.</p>
                <p>Very respectfully, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Irwin</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Rear-Admiral, U. S. Navy,<lb/>Commanding U. S. Naval
                            Force, Pacific Station</hi>.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The <hi rendition="#small-caps">Secretary of the Navy</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Navy Department, Washington, D. C.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
